rationale:
Split into four children with no sibling dependencies.

Why split:
- The selected statement is a conjunction of four logically independent facts with different hypotheses:
  - (i) k ≥ 1 needs only a chart of N;
  - (ii) spt T ⊆ N needs only that U is open, (N̄∖N) ∩ U = ∅, E ⊆ N and T = ∂[[E]];
  - (iii) ∂T = 0 needs only T = ∂[[E]];
  - (iv) is the substantial dimension-zero minimality argument, steps 4.1–4.8 of the parent proof.
- Each child is stated in its natural, reusable generality:
  - C1 holds for any nonempty embedded submanifold;
  - C2 and C3 hold in any ambient dimension P;
  - C4 holds for any set A with spt T ⊆ A.
- Splitting is also forced in practice. `leaf_verification.check_source_delta` lets a leaf append only its own theorem, with no helper declarations and no `set_option`. A complete proof of this node needs about twelve auxiliary declarations.

Assembly (verified in Lean):
1. C1 with (P, d, r, M) = (n+k, n+1, 2, N), using N ≠ ∅ from InClassO, gives n+1 ≤ n+k, hence 1 ≤ k by omega.
2. C2 with the closure condition of InClassO and E ⊆ N gives spt T ⊆ N.
3. C3 gives BoundaryVanishes T.
4. For n = 0, after `subst`, C4 with A := N ∩ U applies, using spt T ⊆ N and support_subset_domain.

This assembly compiles after `import GMT.Ch07.Submission` with the four children as `sorry` stubs. The axioms are propext, Classical.choice and Quot.sound, plus sorryAx coming only from the stubs.

Further checks:
- C1–C3 have complete single-declaration proofs. Each passes the leaf source-delta check, simulated by calling the runtime's own function. Each compiles in place inside the frozen Submission.lean.
- An independent adversarial review checked C4's proof against the exact Lean definitions and found no errors. It covered:
  - the non-measurable M in regularSet;
  - a.e. statements on restricted measures;
  - degree-0 normalisations;
  - every IMRep field of the competitor;
  - all six minimality hypotheses;
  - the definition of massOn.
- The review also produced an end-to-end kernel-checked development of the whole node. I recompiled it: it uses only standard axioms and contains no `sorry`. It is saved in the gitignored GMT/Scratch/regcomp_cop_decomposition/ (Full.lean, Small.lean, Assembly.lean, README.md).
- C4 carries the remaining work. Its own session can split it along the helpers documented there.
- No child name occurs in dag.json or in any of the 1897 git refs.
